<% content_for :title, "Member guide | PT Society" %>
<% content_for :body_class, "help-layout" %>
<main class="help-page">
  <%= render "navigation" %>
  <h1>Member guide</h1>
  <p>Use this guide on your first visit, or choose a task below. You can read it before signing in.</p>
  <nav class="help-contents card" aria-label="On this page">
    <h2>On this page</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="#sign-in">Sign in and sign out</a></li>
      <li><a href="#profile">Finish or edit your profile</a></li>
      <li><a href="#points">Understand points and active status</a></li>
      <li><a href="#events">Find events and save them to your calendar</a></li>
      <li><a href="#check-in">Check in at an event</a></li>
      <li><a href="#submissions">Submit an outside event and follow its status</a></li>
      <li><a href="#troubleshooting">Troubleshooting</a></li>
      <li><a href="#training">Practice with a new member</a></li>
    </ul>
  </nav>
  <section id="sign-in">
    <h2>Sign in and sign out</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Open the club’s website. Choose <strong>Sign up with Google</strong> on your first visit, or <strong>Sign in with Google</strong> when returning.</li>
      <li>Select your <strong>@tamu.edu</strong> Google account. A personal account cannot sign in.</li>
      <li>On your first visit, finish the required profile fields. Returning members go to Home.</li>
      <li>When finished on a shared device, choose <strong>Sign out</strong> in the top navigation.</li>
    </ol>
    <%= render "screenshot", name: "sign-in", caption: "The sign-in page has separate buttons for returning and new members." %>
  </section>
  <section id="profile">
    <h2>Finish or edit your profile</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>For an existing profile, open the menu beside your name and choose <strong>Edit my profile</strong>.</li>
      <li>Enter your first and last names and choose an <strong>Expected graduation</strong> term.</li>
      <li>Choose your <strong>Anticipated application cycle</strong>. These choices are summers, such as Summer 2027.</li>
      <li>Check <strong>I am available to carpool for field trips</strong> if you can help with rides.</li>
      <li>Sharing a phone number is optional. Check <strong>Share my phone number with officers</strong> to show the phone field, then enter a number with 10–15 digits. Spaces, parentheses, dashes, and an initial + are allowed.</li>
      <li>Choose <strong>Save profile</strong>. Look for <strong>Profile saved.</strong> and check your details on Home.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>Turning phone sharing off removes your saved number when you save. Officers can see carpool availability and a shared number, but cannot change your phone number or sharing choice. You cannot change your own role or award yourself points.</p>
    <%= render "screenshot", name: "profile", caption: "Choose a graduation term and a summer application cycle; carpool and phone sharing are optional." %>
  </section>
  <section id="points">
    <h2>Understand points and active status</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Open <strong>Home</strong>. <strong>Total points</strong> shows earned points followed by the semester’s required total.</li>
      <li>Read each required point type separately. Meeting the total alone does not satisfy a missing type minimum.</li>
      <li>Read the status badge and the messages below it. Active membership requires the total, every required type minimum, and paid semester dues.</li>
      <li>If points or dues look wrong, tell an officer the event name, date, and expected point type. Officers record dues; there is no payment checkout in this app.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>Approved outside events and successful attendance check-ins add points. Pending or denied submissions do not. Home shows your own information; regular members cannot open the officer member list.</p>
    <%= render "screenshot", name: "member-home", caption: "Home shows dues and point shortfalls, profile details, and your recent outside-event submissions." %>
  </section>
  <section id="events">
    <h2>Find events and save them to your calendar</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Choose <strong>Events</strong>, or open an upcoming event from Home.</li>
      <li>Open an event to check its location, time, description, point type, and point value.</li>
      <li>Choose <strong>Download .ics</strong> and open the downloaded file in your calendar, or choose <strong>Add to Google Calendar</strong> and save the event there.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>Saving a calendar event does not check you in or award points. If there are no events, check again when officers publish the next meeting.</p>
    <%= render "screenshot", name: "event", caption: "An event’s details include its attendance action and both calendar options." %>
  </section>
  <section id="check-in">
    <h2>Check in at an event</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>At the venue, scan the officer’s QR code, or open the event and choose <strong>Attend Meeting</strong>.</li>
      <li>Sign in and finish your profile if asked. Stay near the meeting location.</li>
      <li>Choose <strong>Check in using my location</strong> and allow this website to use your device’s location.</li>
      <li>Wait for <strong>You’re marked present</strong>. The page shows the points awarded and your updated total.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>The page tells you the allowed distance in feet. Your coordinates are used for the distance check and are not stored with attendance. A second check-in for the same event does not earn a second award.</p>
    <%= render "screenshot", name: "check-in", caption: "The check-in page explains the venue radius and asks for location access." %>
  </section>
  <section id="submissions">
    <h2>Submit an outside event and follow its status</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>On Home, find <strong>Non-PT event submissions</strong> and choose <strong>Submit an event</strong>.</li>
      <li>Enter the event name, the date you attended, a point type, and a description or proof of attendance. The date cannot be in the future. The proof field accepts text; it is not a file upload.</li>
      <li>Choose <strong>Submit for approval</strong>. Look for the confirmation that your submission was sent.</li>
      <li>Return to Home to see the request as <strong>Pending</strong>. The latest ten submissions appear here.</li>
      <li>After review, <strong>Approved</strong> means points were added. <strong>Denied</strong> includes the officer’s reason and adds no points.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>Do not submit the same event and date again to chase an update. Ask an officer about an older request or a correction; the app has no member edit or cancel action for submitted requests.</p>
    <%= render "screenshot", name: "submission", caption: "The outside-event form asks for the name, date, point type, and written description or proof." %>
    <%= render "screenshot", name: "submission-status", caption: "Home lists pending, approved, and denied submissions, including the denial reason." %>
  </section>
  <section id="troubleshooting">
    <h2>Troubleshooting</h2>
    <dl class="help-fixes">
      <dt>Google sign-in fails or chooses the wrong account</dt><dd>Return to the sign-in page and select your @tamu.edu account. If Google reports a service error, retry later. If it reports a redirect or configuration error, send an officer the message and time; changing your profile will not fix it. Never send passwords or sign-in codes.</dd>
      <dt>A profile field is highlighted or saving fails</dt><dd>Use the error links at the top to reach each field. Fill every required field, choose a summer cycle, and correct the phone number if sharing it. Retry after a save error. Previously saved details stay in place until a valid save succeeds.</dd>
      <dt>Location is denied, times out, or says you are too far away</dt><dd>Allow location for this site in your browser’s site settings, enable device location, move closer to the venue, and try again. Use the club’s secure website in your usual browser. Ask an officer to check the event’s coordinates if the problem continues.</dd>
      <dt>Check-in is not configured</dt><dd>Ask the event officer to configure the venue. Reopening or repeatedly submitting the page will not fix missing coordinates.</dd>
      <dt>A submission does not go through</dt><dd>Read the errors, fill all four fields, select an available type, and check the date. If it says you already submitted the event, look on Home. After a connection or server error, check Home before retrying so you do not create another request.</dd>
      <dt>Points are missing or status is still inactive</dt><dd>Check whether a request is still pending or denied, whether a type minimum is missing, and whether dues are recorded. A calendar entry alone earns no points. Refresh Home after a successful review or check-in, then contact an officer with the event details.</dd>
      <dt>A calendar download fails</dt><dd>Return to the event and retry Download .ics. If your browser blocked the download, allow it for this site. Add to Google Calendar is the other available option.</dd>
      <dt>A page is unavailable or you are not authorized</dt><dd>Sign in again and finish your profile. Officer pages require an officer role. If a normal member page still fails, send an officer the page name, message, and time, with private details removed.</dd>
    </dl>
  </section>
  <section id="training" class="card">
    <h2>Practice with a new member</h2>
    <p>Allow about 10 minutes. Have the learner explain each step back to you.</p>
    <ol>
      <li>Sign in with their account and save the required profile details. Let them choose whether to share their phone.</li>
      <li>Find their total, one type minimum, and their dues status on Home. Explain what is still needed to be active.</li>
      <li>Open a published event and save it to a calendar.</li>
      <li>At a real meeting, complete check-in once and find the confirmation.</li>
      <li>Submit a genuine outside event, or explain the form without submitting fictional work. Find its pending status after sending.</li>
      <li>Find the troubleshooting entry for denied location access, then sign out.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>
  <p class="help-review">Checked October 10, 2026. Screenshots use fictional training data. If labels change, tell an officer so the guide can be updated.</p>
</main>
